    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `find_candidates` in `app/catalog.py`. The new test and the existing one pass. I didn't make a live call to the Hub; the test uses a fake API.\n\n```python\ndef find_candidates(name_fragment, task, limit=5, api=None):\n    api = api or HfApi()\n    models = api.list_models(search=name_fragment, pipeline_tag=task, sort=\"downloads\", limit=limit)\n    return [m.id for m in models]\n```\n\n- **One request, done on the Hub:** in the pinned huggingface-hub 2.0.0, `search`, `pipeline_tag`, `sort` and `limit` all go to the Hub as query parameters. The client also stops reading once it has `limit` results, so it doesn't page through anything more.\n- **Most downloaded first:** version 2.0.0 has no `direction` argument, and the Hub sorts from highest to lowest by default, so `sort=\"downloads\"` is all that's needed.\n- **Name match:** `search` matches model ids that contain the fragment, including the owner part (for example `openai/whisper-small` matches \"whisper\").\n- **Extra `api` argument:** I added an optional `api: HfApi | None = None` parameter, the same way `org_models` and `model_stats` work, so tests can pass in a fake. Existing calls that don't pass it work as before.\n- **Test:** I added a test in `tests/test_catalog.py` that checks the exact arguments sent to `list_models` and the order of the returned ids."
